Z||000000||Cheever3000||08-26-2001||10:54 AM||||Last night the Dateline show talked about road rage.  Now I am really upset.  They looked at angry drivers as a problem, rather than asking what stupid crap the other millions of drivers do that <I>makes</I> them angry.  They want to fix the <I>symptom</I>, not the <I>cause</I>.  Get this, on a busy highway, they got in the left ("passing") lane and held it at 65 mph, just to see what would happen!  Can you say DUH?<P>I could turn this into a long raving rant, but you don't wanna hear it.  Besides, my wife is reading this as I type, and disagreeing with me.  Some of you may also.  Here's the place to do it.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||08-26-2001||11:41 AM||||Hey Cheever!<BR>I agree!<BR>It is the discourtous drivers that piss me off...<BR>Worst offenders should be shot on sight...<BR>An armed society is a polite society...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-26-2001||11:49 AM||||Yes I get upset also with those type of drivers But its just not worth the trouble or the stresseverybody needs to stay calm .however I long for the day when you can press an eject button and blow them off the left passing lane <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||EdsB52||08-26-2001||01:45 PM||||Man I agree with you all. I'm toying with moving to Germany or some other European country where they don't ignorantly buy into the fallacy that 65 or 70 is fast. In all reality, 90 or 100 is where the freeway limits should be. This might be a stretch, but restrictive speed limits are, to me, a form of communism. Sounds crazy, but let me argue it. Webster’s defines communism as, "a system of social organization in which all economic and social activity is controlled by a totalitarian state." If few people received speeding tickets and the consensus of people that didn't receive them were happy driving the government-given limits, then you could say our current limits are more socialism. The fact that probably hundreds of thousands of speeding tickets are issued for non-collision related infractions each year denotes, if not outright proves that a good share of the people aren't happy with the government-posted speed limits. Another form of proof I have is the fact that in most major cities, you can drive the freeways and find the average speed limit [(revision, sorry) S/B "speed driven" not speed limit] to be 70-85 in the left lane. And finally, of those that don't receive tickets, many of the remainder are people that want to drive faster, but aren't willing to risk the jeopardy. Communism is primarily referred to as an economic system, but also possesses elements of social control. What I find ironic is the communism-hating conservatives that subscribe to the restrictive speed limits we have, irrespective of the fact they want to drive faster. They're subjecting themselves to, in my opinion, a form of communism while feeling like good American conservative Republicans. If we are a government of the people, for the people, then why are our laws not representative of the wants of the people?<P>“An armed society is a polite society...”<P>What a true statement.<P>“Get this, on a busy highway, they got in the left ("passing") lane and held it at 65 mph, just to see what would happen!”<P>Those ass-wipes. That’s like going to Sturgis on a GSXR and laying 40 yards of scratch (something stock Harleys cannot do) and wondering why everyone wants to kill you! That wasn’t very smart of me, oh well! I can’t stand date rape (Dateline) anyway; the dork that anchors it talks like he’s sitting on the business end of a dildo. If you purposely irritate someone and get thumped, how can you cry foul? I think traffic should be staged, with the left lane around 90-100, #2 lane 80ish, #3 lane 70ish, and #4 lane 55ish (if there are 4 lanes). With more or less lanes the drivers would have to adjust their own staging. The problem with this system is that you can’t legislate common sense, but you can legislate hard numbers, hence, the present crap we have.<P>Jerks that drive 55-65 in the left lane think they're being safe and have this look of, "why is everyone mad at me" when you blow around them. But the collision potential is exponential with drivers like these. I think all people like the left lane because they only have one side to worry about, but that lane is privileged to the faster people.<p>[This message has been edited by EdsB52 (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tonker||08-26-2001||02:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by EdsB52:<BR><B>Webster’s defines communism as, "a system of social organization in which all economic and social activity is controlled by a totalitarian state."</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's because they couldn't be bothered to go research an accurate description of Communism. What they've actually described is Leninism or Stalinism.<P>I agree, though, that the media focuses on the symptoms of road-rage rather than the causes. Then again when someone cuts me off, I don't try to kill them, I flip them the bird and curse at them for a while.||||reg||4
Z||000005||My7Fieros||08-26-2001||03:37 PM||||(clutching my chest)..IM GONNA HAVE A HEART ATTACK!!! I ACTUALLY <B>AGREE</B>w/ Ed!!! and cheever of course...both make very good points! Kudos guys.........<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||4
