Z||000007||Fierowrecker||08-26-2001||06:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>I didn't see the show. Most (all???) of those shows seem to twist things in order to make their predetermined point.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is the biggest problem with the news services...<BR>Instead of unbiased <B>reporting</B>, we get the opinion of what we should think it means...<BR>One reason I listen to shortwave broadcasts from other countries, no overt bias from most of them...<BR>crash...<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||08-27-2001||01:11 AM||||Somebody here brought up the idea of having to "levels" of license's.. say, there could be an 'a' class license with much tougher and more testing, and the requirement to have a well maintained and safe car, and then you can have the privlige to.. well, to go faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  different plates could be used to tell different classes apart.. then again, I think we need to get a safer and better maintained highway system first..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||EdsB52||08-27-2001||01:34 AM||||"well, to go faster  different plates could be used to tell different classes apart.."<P>Unfortunately that wouldn't work because it's the differential of speeds that creates collisions, not the raw speed. For example, if you hit someone at 150mph, will there be damage? Depends, if the person with whom you collided was driving 149 mph in a straight line there would not. Then to exacerbate the situation, the less competent drivers generally cannot establish time/speed/distance with a quick look; they just look for separation without considering rate of closure. Here's our options; let our 80+ year old moms and/or our 16 year old sisters drive and require us to drive down to their competence and ability, or raise the standard of driving competency, rendering fewer, more competent drivers and enjoy few restrictions. Well, since many social aspects of America are communistic and socialistic, we defer to the former. My proposition of staging traffic probably would not work due to the above reasons; the less competent couldn't understand how the simple concept works. I wonder what the rate or ratio of speeding tickets issued to impeding traffic tickets issued is?||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierospeeder||08-27-2001||02:43 AM||||Well when their lincoln was driving in the left lane, they weren't breaking the law.  <P>Until that Black Chevy truck was on their Ass. <P>Theres two sides to view it.  One your obeying the law just like John Wayne, or hey its that guys fault because hes not driving by the "rules", and he's staying in the fast lane.<P>If i was a cop, i would pull everyones ass over.  All those people piss me off.  <P>Doesn't matter if you are driving the speed limit and staying in the slow lane, someones gonna be on your ass.  And if i have to drive faster then the speed limit, how fast should it be??  5mph over, 10, 15 mph???  <BR>20mph so i can kill a pedestrian because i have to get their quicker.  <P>Not to many people think about the consequences when they are speeding, just the cop that pulls you over and says "next time slow the F**k down."<P>If people start ignoring the speedlimit signs, then just ignore the street lights.  Hey its only yellow and what the hell, if i speed up i can make it.  I have seen so many people go through red lights and they had time to stop.  "hey its just a law, if i dont get caught then im not doing anything wrong"<P>You wake up in the morning with roadrage.  Unless someone cuts you off like the movie "roadrage" which was on after that broadcast.  Does Mr. Rogers have roadrage??  When someone cuts him off, will he say, its okay neighbor i understand, you had to get in the exit ramp lane, or would he say"You B*ch, im trying to go to my 2.3million dollar job and im late, heres a taste of some lead."<P>Road rage is caused by the attitudes of people.  try shopping rage at Xmas, your just looking out for your family no one else.  But when theres a UFO invasion like Independence day then we all stick together.  We dont care for others, were looking out for #1, ourselves.  <P>Typical driver, im late for work, i couldn't get my Fat ass up from bed so now im going to kill someone on the road because its their fault that im not going to be on time.  <P>Someone pisses you off on the road, so you have to do something back.  That is the problem with people.  They cant say "who cares".  <P>The ones that wake up with roadrage, driving that SUV that takes up 132 cubed feet of space (est).  The owners that buys them, because they can see over anything.  Meaning hey theres something thats going to happen so i can cut someone else off because i have the advantage. Or the hey i feel safe in it until it rolls over cause i dont know how to drive.  Or the other cars people drive.  But they wake up with the attitude that they "OWN THE ROAD"  thats how it all starts.<P>Blaming someone else for causing roadrage is just BS.<P>On that telecast, they had a guy who was having some roadrage with some 18 year old kid.  Guess he cut him off.  So they were arguing etc...  The guy in the car thinks the teenage is pulling out a gun.  So he grabs his gun and shoots (6-10?) bullets into the teens van.  They show the van and all the bullet holes on the side.  <P>Guess what happens, the guy goes to jail because he kills the teenager's girlfriend that was riding as a passenger.  The cops find no gun in the van.  But the guy states he seen a gun being raised at him which he states on the tv show, but another story he claimed in court.   <P>His reason of shooting, he was put in a situation where he had to use a gun, and if he could change the past, he said he would do it again because he feared for his life and using the gun was his only way of getting out of that situation.  This is a 30some white guy.  I would love for him to get the death penalty, or i would smack his fu head into the wall till he dies.  <P>I guess that dead girl asked for roadrage.  Just a bunch of BS.<P>I ride with my g/f on my motorcycle, i sometimes do 5-10 over the speed limit.  Cops only look for anything over 10 in my area.  I do drive in the slow lane, and even going 10 over isnt good enough for some people.  So they ride my ass, endangering my g/f's life and mine.  But hey, im causing roadrage, and i should pay the penalty.<P>There is a difference between roadrage and speeding.  Theres a place for speeding when your not endangering anyones life (except yours) and theres roadrage when your looking out for yourself.  <P>The people of today are not the same people of the decades of the 50s-70s.  a 50s Xmas a wonderful live, todays Xmas, arnold schwanegar fighting over a toy.  Times has changed and no one is to blame for roadrage just the people who commit it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||JSocha||08-27-2001||11:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by EdsB52:<BR><B>Man I agree with you all. I'm toying with moving to Germany or some other European country where they don't ignorantly buy into the fallacy that 65 or 70 is fast. In all reality, 90 or 100 is where the freeway limits should be. This might be a stretch, but restrictive speed limits are, to me, a form of communism. Sounds crazy, but let me argue it. Webster’s defines communism as, "a system of social organization in which all economic and social activity is controlled by a totalitarian state." If few people received speeding tickets and the consensus of people that didn't receive them were happy driving the government-given limits, then you could say our current limits are more socialism. The fact that probably hundreds of thousands of speeding tickets are issued for non-collision related infractions each year denotes, if not outright proves that a good share of the people aren't happy with the government-posted speed limits. Another form of proof I have is the fact that in most major cities, you can drive the freeways and find the average speed limit [(revision, sorry) S/B "speed driven" not speed limit] to be 70-85 in the left lane. And finally, of those that don't receive tickets, many of the remainder are people that want to drive faster, but aren't willing to risk the jeopardy. Communism is primarily referred to as an economic system, but also possesses elements of social control. What I find ironic is the communism-hating conservatives that subscribe to the restrictive speed limits we have, irrespective of the fact they want to drive faster. They're subjecting themselves to, in my opinion, a form of communism while feeling like good American conservative Republicans. If we are a government of the people, for the people, then why are our laws not representative of the wants of the people?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WOW!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  I can not believe this!  I to actually agree with Ed on this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Lets throw something else into the discussion for support on Eds assertion, that regarding Lidar and the good old fashioned Radar.<P>American society is always taken in by the perpetual cons and scam artists that are out there.  Our government supports and assists in stopping these individuals from taking money unnecessarily from unsuspecting people.<P>Yet, at the same time, in the same breath, our government officials are perpetuating a scam on to us through the issuance of "speeding" tickets.<P>Ever been pulled over and issued a speeding ticket when you in fact new 100% you were not speeding?  Ever tried to contest it?  No win situation unless you have an attorney worth his weight and then some in gold helping you.<P>Lidar and Radar do not have the following ability, to download reports from their system of the transactions during the respective day including date, time and speed stamps.  They do not have a camera/video feature in most cases to show that you were in fact the vehicle being targeted, cloced and subsequently followed.<P>When you go to court, the officer only has to state that he is trainied in the system and that it was calibrated before and after his shift, with no confirmational support as far as a calibration report or witnessed by another individual stating that it was calibrated prior to and at the end of a respective shift.  They only have to indicate that they were in a respective area, noted your vehicle was traveling faster then the rest, indicate the speed, distance and the amount of time they tracked you prior to pulling you over with really no further evidence.<P>You can take the speed, distance (at which he clocked you to the time you passed his position or over the entire distance before you pulled over where the time will be relavent) and the amount of time in your own defense that the officer declared within his testimony to refute his argument, only to have the officers ticket upheld by the court.<P>Also, in most states, LIDAR and RADAR are not under "Judicial Notice" ((or is it Review) Ed, please help me out if I got that term wrong).  Simply stated, this means that the state would have to bring in scientists, researches and everyone else to provide testimony that LIDAR or RADAR works as the manufacturer of these units claim.<P>However, in the end, no matter how you plead your case, the testimony and support you can provide, the attorney you get to fight it, the judge will always side with the state.<P>A former HP from Minot recently wrote a book on "Speeding" and the law after he quit/retired.  <P>In it, he stated that any officer can issue a ticket, regardless if it is correct or not and have it upheld by the court, even if it was issued falsly in the first place to either enhance a future performance review, meet an objective quota to cut down on speeding noted in a particular area or to bring more income into the state.<P>Now doesn't that constitue FRAUD?  If not a state perpetuated and enforced SCAM through the use of legal means to the unsuspecting public?<P>Then they wonder why Road Rage is occuring and only want to treat the symptoms instead of the causes.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||08-27-2001||11:48 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierospeeder:<BR><B>....And if i have to drive faster then the speed limit, how fast should it be??  5mph over, 10, 15 mph???  <BR>20mph so i can kill a pedestrian because i have to get their quicker.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You know all those highway pedestrians have a tendacy to jump on ya lol.  <P>DON'T FORGET THE BOX OF KITTENS!!<P><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cheever3000||08-27-2001||12:02 PM||||Fierospeeder:  First, there <B>is</B> an element of true rage which is definitely a problem on our streets & highways, like that nut with the gun.  I DO NOT condone ANY violent response to a typical case of bad driving .  Second, the show <B>did</B> (briefly) mention that everybody wants to be first in line no matter what, and common courtesy is harder to find.  <P>But they made the assumption that anger is wrong.  All anger is <B>NOT</B> wrong!  I don't even think I need to explain that.<P>And here's the thing my wife and I disagreed on: Yes, it was <I>legal</I> for them to drive only 65 mph in the fast lane.  Her argument is anybody wanting to go faster has no right to be upset at them, and can simply go around them.  ~sigh~ (I tried to reason with her, guys.)  My answer is, first, why obey one rule but disobey the one that says if you're not passing someone then stay to the right?  Geez, stay out of people's way even if they are speeding.  Let <I>them</I> be the troublemakers, not <I>you</I>!  Second, what's right about <I>them</I>(those who drive slow in the fast lane) being inconsiderate to someone wanting to go faster (no matter what their reason for it is)?  What's right about causing accidents by interrupting the flow of traffic and <I>making</I> people weave in & out to go around you?  You can be <B>legal</B>, but still be <B>wrong</B>.  And it can be deadly.  That shows a lot of brains, and makes you a great citizen, huh?  Sure.  Uh-huh, and I'm Mister Rodgers.<P> <p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000014||Voytek||08-27-2001||01:17 PM||||Cheever3000 - I couldn't agree more.<BR>Fierospeeder - why is your name SPEEDER?  Kind of contradictory to what you're saying.<P>I've driven in Germany on the highway a few times.  Even in places with speed limits (yes, they have SOME here and there) people recognize the rules of the road: SLOWER TRAFFIC KEEP RIGHT.  Have you ever seen this sign?  Does it say SLOWER TRAFFIC KEEP RIGHT UNLESS YOU ARE DOING THE SPEED LIMIT?  NO!!!!!!!!!  Move your a$$ over if you're going slower than the guy (or girl) behind you!  Virtually EVERYONE in Germany recognizes this rule instantly.  If you're in the left lane, you get high-beamed a couple of times and YOU BETTER MOVE OVER.  Why are people HERE (N. America) so stupid??<P>That aside, I do not condone unwarranted road rage OR any extremes like, for example, shooting over a traffic argument or people scrapping on the side of the road. HOWEVER, some people do CAUSE road rage.  <P>Fierospeeder - you say that people get pis$ed off when you're too slow for them AND riding in the slower lane.  Well, in this case YOU have the right to get upset - NOT the guy behind you.<P>I agree with most of you here that a vast number of drivers is uneducated and ignorant.  Good drivers are penalized for the bad ones.  EVERYONE speeds occasionally, willingly or not, right or wrong.  If everyone around obeyed all other traffic rules, there would be no road rage and fewer accidents.  Yes, you CAN CAUSE road rage.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||84Bill||08-27-2001||01:51 PM||||I was aiming to run an ass WHOLE off the road today on my way to work. Seems he didnt want to stay behind me in a long line of traffic so he rode down between the lanes and passed on the right and was about to move over right in front of me without enough room. Had he kept going he would have clipped my front quarter and spun out into the median, I REALLY DIDNT CARE if it happend. I'm so sick of this kind of driving! No I wasnt driving my Fiero.<BR>I'm fed up, beware!||||reg||8
