Z||000019||ChadMan||08-27-2001||02:15 PM||||All road rage can easily be avoided by following ChadMan's Courteous Driving Tips!<P>1)  If you're in the left lane on the freeway, check your rearview mirror.  See a bunch of drivers weaving around, looking angry?  Now look in front of you.  See a lot of empty space?  Yes?  OK.  MOVE RIGHT.<P>2)  It's acceptable and often necessary to pull out in front of somebody in busy traffic.  That's a sad reality of city driving.  But if you must pull out in front of another motorist, put the gas pedal on the floor and accelerate hard until you're going as fast as the flow of traffic.  This is called "courtesy."<P>3)  Don't try to merge with freeway traffic unless you're going at least 55 mph.  It just won't work.  Never has.  Never will.<P>4)  Unless you're stuck in gridlock, driving on sheet ice, or passing through a school zone full of children, it is unacceptable to drive slower than 25 mph on a public street.  Ever.  Period.<P>5)  You're waiting in line to turn left at a light and the light turns yellow.  If you're the first car in line, you MUST go when traffic stops.  If you're the third car, sorry, but you CANNOT go - you'll have to wait for the next arrow, you impatient halfwit.  If you're the second car, it's a  judgment call.<P>6a)  Everyone makes mistakes.  If you make one in traffic and another driver is angry with you, shrug and mouth the words "I'm sorry."  Any normal well-adjusted human being will accept your apology and continue on his way.  If the other driver continues berating you, roll down the window and say "Hey, I'm really sorry."  If he STILL keeps berating you, exercise your Second Amendment rights and shoot him in the face.  He deserves it.<P>6b)  You must accept a genuine apology from someone who has wronged you in traffic.  By doing so, you can make the world a better place -- and avoid being shot in the face.||||reg||12
Z||000020||Cheever3000||08-27-2001||02:44 PM||||Good rules, but don't tell <I>us</I>, tell <I>them</I>, cause it's always them, isn't it?  It's never me, noooo!<P>This has nothing to do with road rage, except when I see it happen...  When someone realizes they missed the turn they wanted, or maybe they just changed their mind about where they want to go, they do something really stupid and dangerous, if not outright illegal.    Why don't they just accept the fact that they made a mistake, and find a place to turn around safely?  I see stupid stuff like that almost every single day.<P>Editing cause I need <I>icons</I>...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> <BR>There, now I feel better.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||fierospeeder||08-27-2001||03:39 PM||||im using the name fierospeeder cause im compensating for my 2.5l engine and all the cool names were taken like cliff pennock.<P>There is a difference in speeding and roadrage.   <P>Yes, i do agree about the "rules of the road" i have started a couple of "idiot drivers on the road" threads.  Fast people drive in the left lane, if you are in the fast lane and you see a spoiler thats 10 feet high, let the ricer pass you and get back in the left lane.<P>I have a lot of common sense "rules" of my own on driving such as faster traffic stays left.  If people drove like truckers, with 2 or more second space between each vehicle.  It would eliminate a large majority of traffic jams and the fuel economy would be a lot greater.<P>But people see the car pulled 10 feet so they will accelerate as fast as they can, and jam their brakes just for that 10 feet, instead of driving at a moderate speed.  The brake tapping does cause a chain reaction, and the person behind taps his brake and the person behind etc... and e=mc^2.<P>Eventhough, in my state, it states that obeying the speed limit is the right thing to do.  In the driving manual it states, slower traffic stays right.  Doesn't work when 70% of the stuff in the book isn't used on the road.  <P>When you get old people driving a lincoln in the fast lane, or their car accidently accelerates into a building.  What are you gonna do?  I work at a grocery store (part time), and its amazing to see some of these old people not being able to walk or their hands shaking so much.  or these YUPPIES that even cant read the total from the display to write their check because they down wear glasses and their on the road running over anything they cant see.<P>I do believe in harder testing required to get a drivers license.  Its really easy to get one in illinois.  There should be a more difficult test, with driving school attached and you can get a special license with a tag on your plate stating your a "professional driver"  then you can drive like a cop, driving on the lawn, speeding .....<P>Speed limits, what i have read, were set to 55 to save fuel.  There is a lot of arguments on changing the limit to be higher.  It would be kewl to see how fast a person car can go, and get there quicker, but face the penalty of bad fuel economy.  While half of the people dont care anyway about their fuel economy because they would drive much better.<P>So my point is buy more fieros because these dam scrappage laws are giving people credit to smash their old cars. and dont watch jenny jones while writting a post, too destracting.||||reg||1
Z||000022||JSocha||08-27-2001||04:13 PM||||<OL TYPE=1><BR><LI> In ND (to which V8Fiero and RossT could probably attest to), I drive in the left lane a majority of the time versus the right at any time, irregardless.  The road on that side is much, much better and especially in a Fiero, which is already low to the ground to begin with, makes the drive 100X smoother.  Right lane is nothing more then ND speed bumps, small patches of well {out of-}placed country roads, gas station placed waste oil slicks, tar pits, sink holes and incorrectly placed BUMP AHEAD signs.  With the BUMP AHEAD signs, you brace yourself for the maker marking the bump spot, hit it and wonder if you just ran over the makings of an ant hill.  Mile or two down the road, BAM! your fillings in your teeth practically fall out from an unmarked BUMP.<P><LI> Today's vehicles are built for better gas milage at higher speeds/RPM's.  For example, my 2001 Dodge gets slightly better gas milage at 70 verus 55 via the onboard computer monitor.  Same with my LeBaron and New Yorker.  I can cover the same distance (say a trip from Rugby to Fargo) and have fuel for a return trip at 70 then I could if I drove the same route at 55 where I end up having to refill.<BR></OL>||||reg||1
Z||000023||filthyscarecrow||08-28-2001||08:54 PM||||okay, i teach driver's ed. <BR>i try to teach these kids to think. to react accordingly, and to realise that there are other people trying to get there too, but i doubt it's doing any good. i think driving requires a certain level of intellligence, and a great many of people in this country don't have that. <BR>the attitude i hear the most is that "speed kills" adn "you don't need to drive any faster than i'm going." let ma address the former statement first: speed kills. yes, a faster impact will do more damage. plain and simple. i think we all agree here. what these dopes forget is to factor in the likelihood of an impact based on surrounding traffic. like someone posted before, the person sitting behind you fuming because they can't get by is far more likely to do something monumentally STUPID to get around and in his/her desperation endanger your life and the lives of the kittens in that box. it is less likely that you will lose control of your vehicle because you're doing 85 on the freeway (unless it's raining like a sombitch).<BR>next: "you don't need to drive any faster than i'm going." what most of the trogolodytes who employ this ideology forget is that when they give themselves the right to decide how fast i shuold drive, they hand to me on a silver platter the right to make the decision that maybe they shouldn't be driving at all. maybe they should be sitting upside down in a ditch somewhere. i know how to do it, and i'm sure you do too. it's not that hard. <BR>half the problem is the highway system though. we live in a country that makes the most F*CKING BORING highways in the world. the issue isn't that they don't pay attention, it's that the drive is so coma-inducing that they shut off their brains and forget that the rearview mirrors exist. you should be checking your rearview (especially on the freeway) at LEAST once a minute. people don't realise that cops go 120 to catch speeders adn that 120 is really damn fast when you're only goin 75. (this raises another ethical issue. should cops be allowed to do something FAR FAR More dangerous to catch someone who's only goin a few over? which is the bigger risk?) i've seen people sit in front of ambulences for 5 minutes before they figured it out. personally i think this is one of the worst countries to not only drive in, but live in. no one here respects anyone else anymore. it's rather disgusting, and unfortunately, i'm not immune to it. we want to project our own responsibilities onto others, no matter what the cost. we sue for accidents when we should know damn well that getting into a car is dangerous adn we could be hurt. the risk is the price you pay for the convenience. it seems everyone wants this to be a consequence-free world. it's not going to happen. <BR>kids learn driving habits from parents. i can't pursuade them to respect other people, i can't pursuade them to use their damn blinker, and i can't make them drive like human beings. but if parents would set a decent example, kids would learn from them. <P>til then, i'm mounting james bond missles in the nose and tail of the fiero...||||reg||1
Z||000024||Cheever3000||08-28-2001||11:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>til then, i'm mounting james bond missles in the nose and tail of the fiero...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>That's been done!  I don't remember if it was a Fiero or not, but somebody here posted a link at least a year ago.  Some teenager showed on a website how to do it.  It was great!  Anybody still got that link?<P><BR>||||reg||1
